      "orig": "The expandable command \\inteval takes as its argument an integer expression and produces a result using the normal rules of mathematics with some restrictions, see below. The operations recognized are +, -, * and / plus parentheses. As this command is expandable it can be used where TEX requires a number and for example within a low-level \\edef operation to give a purely numerical result.",
      "text": "The expandable command \\inteval takes as its argument an integer expression and produces a result using the normal rules of mathematics with some restrictions, see below. The operations recognized are +, -, * and / plus parentheses. As this command is expandable it can be used where TEX requires a number and for example within a low-level \\edef operation to give a purely numerical result."
